---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageIntro from '../../components/PageIntro.astro';
import {objectStudies} from '../../lib/objects.js';
import ObjectImage from '../../components/ObjectImage.astro';
const materials=[...new Set(objectStudies.map(object=>object.material))];
---
<Base title="Historical Object Studies" description="Read heraldry on real museum objects: a painted tournament shield, stained glass, Limoges enamel, maiolica, an engraved bookplate, and seal studies, with photographs, accession numbers, evidence ledgers, and research exercises.">
  <PageIntro eyebrow="Heraldry in the material world" title="Arms you can investigate." description={objectStudies.length+' museum objects in paint, glass, enamel, pottery, print, wax, bronze, and manuscript illumination. Ask what an image tells us—and what it leaves unresolved.'}/>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="notice-box"><strong>Begin with the object.</strong><p>These studies reproduce museum photographs of historical artifacts. Dates, identifications, and attributions come from the linked collection records; our visual observations and research questions are editorial teaching notes. Specialist review remains pending.</p></div>
      <div class="lexicon-top" style="margin-top:35px"><div><p class="eyebrow"><span class="star">✦</span> The first object-study collection</p><h2 class="small-title">A photograph is a beginning.</h2></div><span id="object-count" class="smallcaps" role="status">{objectStudies.length} objects shown</span></div>
      <div class="gallery-filter" role="group" aria-label="Filter objects by material">
        {['All objects',...materials].map((material,i)=><button class:list={['chip',i===0&&'active']} type="button" data-material={material} aria-pressed={i===0}>{material}</button>)}
      </div>
      <div class="object-grid">
        {objectStudies.map(object=><article class="object-card" data-object data-material={object.material}>
          <a class="object-plinth" href={'/objects/'+object.id+'/'} aria-label={'Study '+object.catalogueTitle}><ObjectImage object={object}/></a>
          <div class="object-body"><span class="smallcaps">{object.culture} · {object.date}</span><h2><a href={'/objects/'+object.id+'/'}>{object.title}</a></h2><p>{object.summary}</p>{'studyType' in object&&<p class="caption">{object.studyType}</p>}<p class="object-accession">{object.museum}<br/>Accession {object.accession}</p><a class="text-link" href={'/objects/'+object.id+'/'}>Open the object study ↗</a></div>
        </article>)}
      </div>
      <div class="object-comparison">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="star">✦</span> A comparative workshop</p><h2 class="small-title">One language. Different evidence.</h2><p>Compare how each material changes the questions you need to ask.</p>
        <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Object comparison table"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Object</th><th scope="col">Start by observing</th><th scope="col">Then investigate</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row"><a href="/objects/franconian-targe/">Painted targe</a></th><td>Physical outline and painted achievement</td><td>Alternative family attribution and the reverse decoration</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><a href="/objects/heraldic-glass/">Stained-glass shield</a></th><td>Colour areas and structural joins</td><td>Lighting, conservation, and original setting</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><a href="/objects/halewyn-ghistele-enamel/">Impalement in enamel</a></th><td>Two armorial compositions joined vertically</td><td>Patronage, workshop attribution, and possible larger ensemble</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><a href="/objects/vitelleschi-maiolica/">Arms on maiolica</a></th><td>A central shield within an ornamental border</td><td>Family identification, circle attribution, and the unknown commission</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><a href="/objects/cary-bookplate/">An engraved bookplate</a></th><td>Armorial display, name, and engraver’s inscription</td><td>Catalogue date range and evidence of actual use in a book</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><a href="/objects/lowlands-wax-seal/">Armorial wax impression</a></th><td>A shield, helmet, ornament, and separate mount</td><td>Material colour, catalogue uncertainty, and missing documentary context</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><a href="/objects/ghent-style-matrix/">A later pictorial matrix</a></th><td>Opposite arrangements on matrix and accompanying impression</td><td>Manufacture date, medieval style, and the impression’s separate history</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><a href="/objects/simon-de-varie/">An illuminated French leaf</a></th><td>Lettered scrolls, a portrait, and several armorial forms</td><td>Transcription, normalization, and reported overpainting</td></tr>
        </tbody></table></div>
        <p>Choose one claim about each object. Write down its source, what it establishes, and what additional evidence would change your confidence. A catalogue attribution and a visible feature should not receive the same kind of explanation.</p>
        <p><a href="/objects/seals/" class="btn btn-line">Try the seal evidence workshop ↗</a></p>
        <p><a href="/transcription-desk/" class="btn btn-line">Read a manuscript at the transcription desk ↗</a></p>
        <p><a href="/objects/compare/" class="btn btn-dark">Compare objects and keep research notes ↗</a></p>
        <a href="/seminars/05-material-culture/" class="text-link">Continue to the material-culture seminar ↗</a>
      </div>
      <p class="caption">Images: The Metropolitan Museum of Art, Cleveland Museum of Art, and The J. Paul Getty Museum, Open Access / Open Content (CC0). Individual credit lines and source-image links appear in each study. Broader repository and regional coverage is still needed.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/armorial/">Explore the original teaching shields ↗</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <script>
    const filters=document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-material]:not([data-object])');
    const cards=document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-object]');
    const status=document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#object-count');
    filters.forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',()=>{
      let count=0;
      cards.forEach(card=>{card.hidden=button.dataset.material!=='All objects'&&card.dataset.material!==button.dataset.material;if(!card.hidden)count++;});
      filters.forEach(filter=>{filter.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(filter===button));filter.classList.toggle('active',filter===button);});
      if(status)status.textContent=count+' object'+(count===1?'':'s')+' shown';
    }));
  </script>
  <style>
    .object-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:24px;margin:25px 0 45px}
    .object-card{border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--white);min-width:0}
    .object-plinth{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;height:300px;padding:22px;background:var(--paper-2)}
    .object-plinth :global(img){width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:contain}
    .object-body{padding:24px}.object-body h2{font:500 1.9rem/1.1 var(--serif);margin:13px 0}.object-body p{color:var(--ink-2);font-size:.86rem}
    .object-accession{font-size:.73rem!important;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:16px}.object-body .smallcaps{color:var(--red)}
    .object-comparison{background:var(--paper-2);border:1px solid var(--line);padding:clamp(20px,4vw,42px);margin-bottom:30px}
    .table-scroll{overflow-x:auto;margin:25px 0}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;min-width:560px;font-size:.85rem}th,td{padding:15px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}th a{text-decoration:underline}
    @media(max-width:900px){.object-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.object-plinth{height:330px}}
  </style>
</Base>
